# Line endings (cross-platform task, PR 3): every text file is checked out with LF on every platform, also with
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows; compressed records, images and data files are binary.
* text eol=lf
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.root binary
*.dat binary
*.npz binary
*.cells binary
*.readout binary
*.t07data binary
# Upload package (maintainer decision, 2026-11-14: "Exclude tests/ except runtime needs"). `git archive HEAD:plugins/hep-research`
# reads attributes only from the archived tree, so these lines live here, not in a repository-root .gitattributes. Every
# path under tests/ is left out of the uploaded zip, which keeps it inside the documented limits (5,000 files, 200 MB),
# except what shipped code reads at runtime. The last matching line wins, and git archive skips a whole folder whose
# own path is export-ignore, so each kept file's folders are unset as well. tools/check_packaging.py measures this
# archive and fails when a shipped reference into tests/ does not resolve inside it.
/tests/** export-ignore
# folders that hold kept files
/tests/examples -export-ignore
/tests/skills -export-ignore
/tests/skills/hep_detector -export-ignore
/tests/adapters -export-ignore
/tests/adapters/fixtures -export-ignore
/tests/adapters/fixtures/cr_propagation -export-ignore
/tests/adapters/fixtures/cr_propagation/e1 -export-ignore
# the tests that profile capabilities cite (contracts/registry.py requires them), with the modules they import
/tests/__init__.py -export-ignore
/tests/_outputs.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/__init__.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/test_ams_flux_ratio.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/test_eic_profile_routing.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/test_collider_angular.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/test_detector_resolution_and_recasting.py -export-ignore
/tests/examples/test_qed_prediction.py -export-ignore
/tests/skills/__init__.py -export-ignore
